\section{ What is the purpose of \texttt{SIGCHLD} and \texttt{SIGCHLD} according to the man page?}
(from \texttt{man 7 signal})
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{@{} l c p{9cm} @{}}
\toprule
\textbf{Signal} & \textbf{Default} & \textbf{Purpose} \\ \midrule
\texttt{SIGCHLD} & Ign &
Delivered to a parent when a child process stops or terminates, allowing the
parent to call \texttt{wait()/waitpid()} and reap the child. \\[4pt]
\texttt{SIGQUIT} & Core &
Generated from the controlling terminal (usually
\texttt{Ctrl+\textbackslash}). Terminates the process and produces a core dump
for debugging. \\ \bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

