\section{How is the SIGINT (CTRL-C) signal handler set up in main()}

\begin{lstlisting}[language=C, caption={Setting up the CTRL-C handler}]
 /* Create a signal handler for CTRL-C which is SIGINT */
  signal(SIGINT, ctrlc_handler);
\end{lstlisting}

The call to \lstinline|signal()| registers \lstinline|ctrlc_handler| as the
handler for \texttt{SIGINT}.  When the user presses \texttt{Ctrl+C}, the kernel
delivers \texttt{SIGINT}; the handler increments the global counter
\lstinline|ctrlc_hit| and prints how many times the signal has been received.

