\section{How does the code tell select() to watch stdin for activity?}

\begin{lstlisting}[language=C]
FD_ZERO(&readmask);
FD_ZERO(&writemask);
FD_ZERO(&exceptmask);

FD_SET(0, &readmask);    /* watch stdin for readable data */
FD_SET(0, &exceptmask);  /* watch stdin for exceptional conditions */
\end{lstlisting}

Placing file descriptor~0 in \lstinline|readmask| causes \texttt{select()} to
return when keyboard input arrives; adding it to \lstinline|exceptmask| allows
the program to handle exceptional states (e.g.\ hang-up).

